* Bruise
* Scrape
* Sprain
* Cut
* Burn
* Break
* Fracture

Bruise,A dark mark on the skin caused by a blow or impact that 
ruptures blood vessels but doesn't break the skin.
Moretón / Cardenal,
I have a large purple bruise on my thigh from where I bumped into the table

Scrape,"A minor injury where the top layer of skin is rubbed or torn off, 
usually by sliding against a rough surface.
",Raspadura / Raspón
The runner fell on the gravel and got a nasty scrape on his elbow.


Sprain,An injury to a joint (like an ankle or wrist) caused by a sudden
twist that stretches or tears ligaments.
,Torcedura / Esguince,
She couldn't play in the game because she suffered a severe ankle sprain during practice."""


Cut,"A break or opening in the skin or flesh, typically caused by a sharp
object like a knife or glass."
,Corte / Herida,
Be careful with that sharp knife; you don't want to get a cut on
your finger."""

Burn,"Damage to the skin or other tissues caused by heat, chemicals, 
electricity, or radiation.",
Quemadura,
forgot to wear oven mitts and got a small burn on my hand from the tray."""


Break,A general term for a bone that has been cracked or separated into
two or more pieces.
,Rotura / Fractura,
"""He had to wear a cast for six weeks after he managed to break his 
leg while skiing."""
Fracture,The medical term for a break in a bone; it can range from a
thin crack to a complete snap.
,Fractura,"
""The X-ray confirmed a hairline fracture in her wrist, 
even though it didn't look broken."""
